# The toolchain the Aether port is built and tested against. Pins are what
# was last verified, not "latest"; bump one in the commit that needs it (or
# that re-verified the port against it), as the other Aether repos do.
#
# Install both in one step (aeb's get.sh, pinned):
#   curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aether-lang-dev/aeb/main/get.sh \
#     | AE_PIN=$AE_PIN AEB_REF=$AEB_REF sh
#
# 0.909.0 (2026-11-12): the first pin. contrib.quickjs (quickjs-ng 0.17.0)
# is the engine; std.worker's run_detached gives a tool call its thread,
# std.sync its completion flag, std.os's spawn_proc_to a bash process group.
# Verified: aeb .tests.ae (20 suites, 156 tests, workspace.sh, check_layers.sh)
# on macOS arm64, ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04, kernel 5.15: no Landlock ABI 2, bash
# runs unsandboxed there as upstream) and cachyos (kernel 7.3: Landlock holds).
# Session + provider slice (2026-11-12), same pins: aeb .tests.ae green (35 suites)
# on macOS arm64, ae-x64 and cachyos; ae/tests/upstream-e2e.sh gives the same
# results on all three, except test_sandbox's workspace cases on ae-x64
# (kernel 5.15, no Landlock ABI 2: bash runs unsandboxed there, as upstream).
# 0.912.0 (2026-11-13): `import std.os hiding (...)` (0.911.0, aether #3653)
# makes "only tools/process, tools/jail and tui/open's launch start a program"
# a compile error (E0304) instead of a check_layers grep; the 0.910.0 fixes
# (aether #3655: a returned local optional owning a string, a local read once
# in a loop) let ae/term's surface loops store one blank again. std.posix.regex
# (#3654, 0.912.0) is not used. Verified: aeb .tests.ae, tools/tui_tests.sh and
# ae/tests/upstream-e2e.sh on macOS arm64, ae-x64 and cachyos.
# 0.914.0 (2026-11-14): aether #3694 fixes six asks and more (push of a call result,
# qualified slice locals, basename collision on qualified types, ptr as string,
# ipc SIGPIPE, run_stdio stderr_to/cwd, `ae run` exit on a failing spec); their
# stand-ins are removed in the same commit.
# 0.915.0 (2026-11-14): std.fs's stat (inode, mode, ns mtime), flock, O_EXCL,
# fd ops and positional writes, std.os.environ and signal_watch, std.io.set_echo
# replace nib.sysgap, which is deleted.
# 0.916.0 (2026-11-14): contrib.quickjs gains eval_async, a host deadline with
# cancel and stop cells, promise_state/promise_result and a to_string that
# returns (string, error); quickjs-ng 0.18.0. nib.qjsgap is deleted.
# 0.923.0 (2026-11-18): fs.unlink and fs.create_dir_with_mode return
# (ok, kind, msg), and std.fs has KIND_READ_ONLY_FS, KIND_BUSY and
# KIND_FILE_TOO_BIG (aether #3728); /undo's stat guess and fserr's POSIX errno
# numbers are gone. Verified: aeb .tests.ae 89/89 on macOS arm64 with the
# installed release.
# 0.931.0 (2026-11-20): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive needed and no
# source change. Verified: aeb .tests.ae on macOS arm64 (88 of 89; the red-team
# script's sockets need a checkout path under about 70 characters, and it passed
# 200 checks from a short path) and on ae-x64 (88 of 89 the same way; passed from
# a short path; ae/tests/llm_test.ae failed once under heavy load and passes alone).
# No provider traffic: mocks and fixtures only.
AE_PIN=0.931.0

# v0.344 (2026-11-12): aether.program and aether.program_test with lib().
